From alobo at ija.csic.es  Fri Apr  4 11:26:21 2003
From: alobo at ija.csic.es (Agustin Lobo)
Date: Fri Apr  4 11:26:21 2003
Subject: [STATSGRASS] gstat and grass raster null values
Message-ID: <Pine.OSF.3.91.1030404170848.4995G-100000@paleo.ija.csic.es>

Apparentely, gstat does not
handle grass null values. At least, 
I've found problems with gstat
if null values are not masked out.

Therefore,
it's important to set a proper mask.
Something like:
r.mapcalc "MASK = if(isnull(raster),null(),1)"

will create a MASK for null values
or inlude them in the active mask.

Also, thanks to Edzer, Im using
the following line command style for gstat
in grass scripts:

gstat -e semivariogram -c $cut -i $wid dum > $nout

Hope this helps (and that I'm not wrong).

Agus

